               <t:note>
              
                  <t:ab type="history">Bur was a large historical region, across the present Ethio-Eritrean border. It was divided into upper Bur and lower Bur.
                     Its territory covers parts of <t:placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC1236Agama">ʿAgāma</t:placeName>, the entire <t:placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC1298Akkala">Akkälä Guzay</t:placeName> 
                     and lands further to the east, including perhaps <t:placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC2023Buri">Buri</t:placeName>. 
                     In the first half of the 15th century, <t:placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC2019Bur">Bur</t:placeName>
                     seems to have been ruled by a <t:roleName type="office">śǝyyum (šum)</t:roleName>, whom 
                     <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS10626ZaraY">
                        <t:roleName type="office">ʾaṣe</t:roleName>
                     </t:persName> 
                     <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS10626ZaraY">Zarʾa Yāʿqob</t:persName>
                     put under the supermacy of the <t:roleName type="office">baḥǝra nagāš</t:roleName> along with the governor of <t:placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC5749Sire">Šire</t:placeName>, <t:placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC3764Hamase">Ḥamāsen</t:placeName> and 
                        <t:placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC5575Saraye">Sarāye</t:placeName>.
                    
                        
                        
                        </t:ab>
               </t:note>
               
               
               
               
